* The ability animations are based on and are affected by {{M|status resistance}}. This affects the following things:
** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|StatusResistance<sub>1</sub> > StatusResistance<sub>2</sub>}}
*** The leash disappears, and the primary target is no longer affected by Soulbind.
*** However, the secondary target is still affected by Soulbind's effects.
** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|StatusResistance<sub>2</sub> > StatusResistance<sub>1</sub>}}
*** The chain disappears, and the secondary target is no longer affected by Soulbind.
*** The primary target is still affected by Soulbind, and leashes the next valid enemy hero within the search radius.

* The ability's {{M|leash}} mechanic has the following properties:
** [[Movement Speed#Set Movement Speed|Sets]] the affected enemy unit's current {{M|movement speed}} as fixed value upon applying the leash {{M|debuff}}.
*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|Set[[Movement Speed|MS]] {{=}} CurrentMS}}
** Soulbind applies a 4 set movement speed reduction to either units per 1-distance away between both units, up to a min 0.1-set movement speed value.
** Hence, the ability formulas are defined as:
*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|When 0 < [[Wikipedia:Absolute_value|{{!}}]](PrimaryTargetPosition - SecondaryTargetPosition)[[Wikipedia:Absolute_value|{{!}}]] < 594.975, Set[[Movement Speed|MS]] {{=}} 2380 - 4 × [[Wikipedia:Absolute_value|{{!}}]](PrimaryTargetPosition - SecondaryTargetPosition)[[Wikipedia:Absolute_value|{{!}}]]}}
*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|When 594.975 < [[Wikipedia:Absolute_value|{{!}}]](PrimaryTargetPosition - SecondaryTargetPosition)[[Wikipedia:Absolute_value|{{!}}]] < 780, Set[[Movement Speed|MS]] {{=}} 0.1}}
*** The set movement speed value along the edges does not decrease below the original movement speed.
